WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:03.236
14 defeats and now a late night

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:04.671
near rumble.

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:05.972
Kevin McCarthy

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:07.340
has that passed him

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:08.208
and he is now

00:00:08.208 --> 00:00:10.343
speaker of the House

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:10.910
Did you hear him

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.545
say when he got up there.

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:14.147
I never thought I would get up here.

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:15.081
I mean there was that moment

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:17.717
and you contrast that to the confidence

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:19.753
that he exuded all day long all week.

00:00:19.986 --> 00:00:20.320
Maybe

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:22.122
it was sort of a feigned appearance

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:24.124
to just kind of have a stiff upper lip.

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:27.060
But in reality, he until that moment,

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.261
I think we were all thinking,

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:30.296
will he actually become the speaker

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:31.131
of the House,

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:33.133
including, of course, a brawl.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.169
Almost, almost, almost a brawl.

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:37.237
I mean, the

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:41.007
the quickness with which he was elated

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:42.709
and then he was

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:44.611
defeated and deflated

00:00:44.611 --> 00:00:46.246
and then he was angry.

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:47.380
And then all of a sudden,

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:50.850
they convinced the at least

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:53.653
Matt Gates and for others

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:54.988
to change their votes

00:00:54.988 --> 00:00:56.823
to vote present to lower the threshold

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:58.758
so that he could actually become speaker.

00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:00.960
And to see him run down to the well

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:02.729
and say, hold on,

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:03.630
we don't want to adjourn.

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:05.231
All the red cards coming out.

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:05.498
Yeah.

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:06.166
I mean, it was

00:01:06.166 --> 00:01:09.002
it was truly, truly dramatic.

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:10.370
I mean, we talked about this

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:11.304
being a historic

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:13.206
once in a century occurrence.

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:15.241
I think this will go down in history

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:16.643
for so many reasons,

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:18.778
not the least of which the 15 rounds

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:19.112
it took

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:20.914
to become the Speaker of the House.

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:23.817
The idea of all of the negotiating

00:01:23.817 --> 00:01:25.919
and the jockeying behind the scenes.

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:28.488
But immediately it was as if the

00:01:28.488 --> 00:01:28.922
of course,

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:31.024
Minority Leader Hakeem Jeffries,

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:31.858
all of whom

00:01:31.858 --> 00:01:33.193
now are congresspersons

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:34.861
officially and longer elect

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:36.196
they knew where to pick up

00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:38.531
just as McCarthy did, which is the the

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:39.666
the contrast

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:41.601
what the Democrats and the Republicans

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.670
would now do going forward. Yeah.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:45.572
And it also went from chaos

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:47.474
to the typical pageant

00:01:47.474 --> 00:01:49.943
pageantry and protocol that we

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:51.978
are used to seeing

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:53.646
when a new Congress begins.

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:54.013
It just

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:56.549
is it usually at one 45 in the morning,

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:57.617
although it is toast.

00:01:57.617 --> 00:01:58.852
It is January 7th.

00:01:58.852 --> 00:01:59.986
And this is around

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:01.688
I mean, small hours the morning.

00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:02.522
Right, of what happened

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:03.857
when two years ago

00:02:03.857 --> 00:02:06.993
on that sober anniversary they were all

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:08.228
Americans are really watching

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:10.330
what would happen in these very chambers.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:11.865
I would go right now to Melanie

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:13.867
Zona who is on Capitol Hill.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:14.701
Melanie,

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:16.469
you have been holding down the fort

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:18.838
over there. What happens next tonight?

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:20.306
If you can predict anything

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:21.508
at this point,

00:02:21.508 --> 00:02:23.009
your members are going to go home

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:25.044
and get a lot of sleep, myself included.

00:02:25.078 --> 00:02:26.012
Hopefully,

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:27.180
look, what's happening

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:28.948
next is they need to organize the house.

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:29.749
So they need to pass

00:02:29.749 --> 00:02:31.518
what's known as a rules package.

00:02:31.518 --> 00:02:32.352
But we are hearing that

00:02:32.352 --> 00:02:33.353
they are going to wait

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:34.420
until Monday to do that.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:35.722
They've had agreement

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:37.357
now after all of this resolution

00:02:37.357 --> 00:02:39.692
with the speaker standoff.

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:40.760
And I just want to step back

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.896
for a moment, because for Kevin McCarthy,

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:44.697
this has been a lifelong dream.

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:46.399
He was working in politics.

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:47.901
His entire adult life.

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:50.970
He was denied the speakership in 20, 15.

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:53.373
He worked to court the conservative wing

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:54.207
ever since then.

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:55.308
He immediately got to work.

00:02:55.308 --> 00:02:56.075
Strategizing is

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:58.411
how can I get the speakership one day?

00:02:58.411 --> 00:02:59.946
And that is the moment we are in

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:01.414
after this messy, ugly

00:03:01.414 --> 00:03:02.582
confrontation today.

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:03.917
All week, it was a rollercoaster.

00:03:03.917 --> 00:03:05.852
He finally got there.

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:07.353
But this is going to be a position

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:09.389
that is significantly weaker

00:03:09.389 --> 00:03:10.023
than the one

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:10.990
he probably envisioned

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:13.059
because in order to get the gavel,

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:14.227
he had to negotiate,

00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:16.429
negotiate away so much of his power

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:17.597
And we still don't know

00:03:17.597 --> 00:03:19.065
the full scope of the concessions

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:19.866
that he gave way.

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:21.901
I did catch up with Matt Gates briefly

00:03:22.402 --> 00:03:24.237
to ask him what made him change his vote.

00:03:24.237 --> 00:03:24.871
All he said is

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:27.173
I ran out of things to ask for

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:27.707
You know, there's

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:29.175
there were swirling

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:30.143
rumors swirling around

00:03:30.143 --> 00:03:30.977
that he may have been given

00:03:30.977 --> 00:03:31.878
a subcommittee gavel.

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:33.479
Kevin McCarthy denied that.

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:34.480
And Kevin McCarthy

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.783
did already gave so much away,

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:37.951
including this tool known

00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:38.818
as the motion to vacate

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:39.953
the speaker's chair,

00:03:39.953 --> 00:03:41.321
which means any single member

00:03:41.321 --> 00:03:42.555
can call for a vote

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:43.790
to oust the sitting speaker.

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:45.291
So going forward, yes,

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:46.159
Kevin McCarthy has gotten

00:03:46.159 --> 00:03:46.793
the speakership,

00:03:46.793 --> 00:03:48.628
but the task, the tough task

00:03:48.628 --> 00:03:50.096
now begins and that's governing.

00:03:50.096 --> 00:03:51.898
And as we saw, it is going to be messy.

00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:53.333
It is going to be difficult.

00:03:53.333 --> 00:03:55.301
He has these warring wings of his party

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:56.669
that he is going to have to contend

00:03:56.669 --> 00:03:58.271
with every single day.

00:03:58.271 --> 00:04:00.306
Every single vote is going to be a battle

00:04:00.306 --> 00:04:00.807
and a fight.

00:04:00.807 --> 00:04:02.075
And so that is what we can expect

00:04:02.075 --> 00:04:03.243
for the next two years

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:03.676
as Speaker

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:05.845
Kevin McCarthy takes the gavel.

00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:06.412
I mean, Melanie,

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:07.714
I'm pretty sure that you've

00:04:07.714 --> 00:04:08.881
won the negotiation

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:09.749
when you literally

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:11.484
have run out of things to ask for

00:04:11.484 --> 00:04:12.252
and the other person

00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:14.187
is just giving you the yeses.

00:04:14.187 --> 00:04:16.189
I do wonder what the scope of everything

00:04:16.189 --> 00:04:18.091
they've actually been able to concede

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:20.193
and get what that will ultimately be.

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:21.561
But as we're waiting to hear again

00:04:21.561 --> 00:04:23.062
from the new speaker of the House

00:04:23.062 --> 00:04:24.197
when he'll address reporters

00:04:24.197 --> 00:04:25.365
outside of his office

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:26.799
we're getting some new reporting in

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:28.901
about what happened during that.

00:04:29.202 --> 00:04:30.536
Very and we'll just call it

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:32.305
a heated moment that everyone leaned

00:04:32.305 --> 00:04:33.406
into their television screens

00:04:33.406 --> 00:04:35.875
to watch during that failed 14 vote.

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:37.944
What can you tell us about that moment?

00:04:37.944 --> 00:04:40.246
That was just such an incredible moment.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:42.148
I've been covering the Congress

00:04:42.148 --> 00:04:42.649
for ten years.

00:04:42.649 --> 00:04:44.183
I have never seen anything like that

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:44.851
on the House floor.

00:04:44.851 --> 00:04:46.352
Before, but we are learning new details,

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:47.587
thanks to my colleague Andy Greer,

00:04:47.587 --> 00:04:48.755
who is in the chamber

00:04:48.755 --> 00:04:50.923
and was also working her sources

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:51.991
to figure out what happened.

00:04:51.991 --> 00:04:53.960
And in this moment,

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:55.228
that moment is when

00:04:55.228 --> 00:04:56.429
Kevin McCarthy realized

00:04:56.429 --> 00:04:57.864
that he wasn't going to have the votes

00:04:57.864 --> 00:04:59.666
because Rosendale had voted present.

00:04:59.666 --> 00:05:00.600
And so

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.635
Kevin McCarthy was completely dejected.

00:05:02.669 --> 00:05:03.136
You saw him

00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:03.603
walk up

00:05:03.603 --> 00:05:04.604
the aisle towards

00:05:04.604 --> 00:05:06.272
where Boebert and Gates were sitting

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:08.641
and pleading with them to vote for him.

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:10.977
He was in a moment of desperation.

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:12.712
And then you saw Mike Rogers

00:05:12.712 --> 00:05:14.947
coming up from behind the well

00:05:14.947 --> 00:05:16.382
coming down the aisle.

00:05:16.382 --> 00:05:18.651
And this is someone he's a chairman.

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:21.387
He is a close McCarthy ally.

00:05:21.387 --> 00:05:23.356
He's been growing more frustrated

00:05:23.356 --> 00:05:24.123
and more frustrated

00:05:24.123 --> 00:05:25.258
with the holdouts all week.

00:05:25.258 --> 00:05:26.359
So that is important context.

00:05:26.359 --> 00:05:26.993
In fact,

00:05:26.993 --> 00:05:28.861
we are told that he had threatened

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:29.662
to kick

00:05:29.662 --> 00:05:30.396
some of the holdouts

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:32.265
off of their committee assignments

00:05:32.265 --> 00:05:33.333
if they didn't fall in line.

00:05:33.333 --> 00:05:35.201
So he was so frustrated.

00:05:35.201 --> 00:05:36.402
He came down the aisle

00:05:36.402 --> 00:05:37.670
and sources told Annie Greer

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:38.671
that he basically said,

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:41.240
Matt, you're finished to him

00:05:41.274 --> 00:05:42.675
at that point.

00:05:42.675 --> 00:05:44.310
Hudson, another member

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:45.912
came up behind him, sort of muzzled

00:05:45.912 --> 00:05:47.046
him and tried to hold him back

00:05:47.046 --> 00:05:48.815
so he wasn't able to speak any more.

00:05:48.815 --> 00:05:50.783
But it really spoke to the moment of just

00:05:50.783 --> 00:05:52.318
how tense things were

00:05:52.318 --> 00:05:52.985
and how it looked like

00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:54.554
it was all falling apart

00:05:54.554 --> 00:05:55.922
for Kevin McCarthy,

00:05:55.922 --> 00:05:57.190
but only almost as quickly

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:57.957
as it fell apart.

00:05:57.957 --> 00:05:58.958
Things then came together.

00:05:58.958 --> 00:06:00.460
We're told that leadership was

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:02.395
then informed that Gates was a yes,

00:06:02.395 --> 00:06:03.763
and then there were instead of motioning

00:06:03.763 --> 00:06:04.630
to adjourn,

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:05.832
there's another moment of chaos

00:06:05.832 --> 00:06:06.733
where they switched their votes

00:06:06.733 --> 00:06:07.367
and they were deciding

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:08.868
to do another speaker vote.

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:10.036
And then what ends up happening

00:06:10.036 --> 00:06:11.137
is every single

00:06:11.137 --> 00:06:11.938
one of those remaining

00:06:11.938 --> 00:06:13.439
holdouts voted present.

00:06:13.439 --> 00:06:15.608
So just a complete rollercoaster

00:06:15.608 --> 00:06:17.777
of a vote of a day of a week, really.

00:06:17.777 --> 00:06:19.312
Ever since the midterms, this

00:06:19.312 --> 00:06:20.646
has been a rollercoaster

00:06:20.646 --> 00:06:21.381
for Kevin McCarthy.

00:06:21.381 --> 00:06:22.682
So a huge sigh of relief

00:06:22.682 --> 00:06:24.617
for him and his allies tonight.

00:06:24.617 --> 00:06:25.284
Hey, listen, Mayor,

00:06:25.284 --> 00:06:26.719
adjourning right now, Melanie,

00:06:26.719 --> 00:06:27.787
we're watching them on

00:06:27.787 --> 00:06:28.654
with their emotion.

00:06:28.654 --> 00:06:31.758
There are two in favor of the 118th

00:06:31.758 --> 00:06:33.926
Congress now sworn into office

00:06:33.926 --> 00:06:35.328
going home tonight.

00:06:36.796 --> 00:06:37.930
Let's listen in.

00:06:42.034 --> 00:06:42.602
Well, here

00:06:42.602 --> 00:06:43.102
is right now

00:06:43.102 --> 00:06:44.370
in the studio, we've got CNN chief

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:46.172
White House correspondent Phil Mattingly,

00:06:46.172 --> 00:06:46.839
Tim Mitchell,

00:06:46.839 --> 00:06:48.107
a Washington correspondent

00:06:48.107 --> 00:06:50.243
for the Atlanta Journal Constitution,

00:06:50.243 --> 00:06:50.877
and Liam

00:06:50.877 --> 00:06:51.911
Donovan, former

00:06:51.911 --> 00:06:52.945
National Republican

00:06:52.945 --> 00:06:54.947
Senatorial Committee aide.

00:06:55.381 --> 00:06:57.083
This is pretty amazing right now,

00:06:57.083 --> 00:06:59.685
just the idea of being muzzled on that

00:06:59.685 --> 00:07:01.721
on the actual house of the floor,

00:07:01.721 --> 00:07:02.321
the threat.

00:07:02.321 --> 00:07:03.423
What do you guys make of it?

00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:04.657
I mean, that's just a good friend

00:07:04.657 --> 00:07:05.825
right off the.

00:07:05.825 --> 00:07:09.262
Knowing where that was going to head

00:07:09.262 --> 00:07:10.830
the beauty of Mel's breakdown

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:12.465
is how eloquently she was going through

00:07:12.465 --> 00:07:13.232
very complex

00:07:13.232 --> 00:07:13.966
details of what

00:07:13.966 --> 00:07:15.501
we've seen over the last four days.

00:07:15.501 --> 00:07:17.804
I'll try and simplify it to some degree.

00:07:17.804 --> 00:07:18.905
And I think at this table,

00:07:18.905 --> 00:07:20.640
we probably have several decades

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:21.507
of experience covering

00:07:21.507 --> 00:07:22.708
Capitol Hill and covering

00:07:22.708 --> 00:07:24.243
that chamber in particular.

00:07:24.243 --> 00:07:26.112
Nothing about the last four days

00:07:26.112 --> 00:07:27.213
was normal.

00:07:27.213 --> 00:07:29.115
Everything about the last 10 hours

00:07:29.115 --> 00:07:30.750
was extraordinary.

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:34.120
And the biggest question now is, is this

00:07:34.287 --> 00:07:36.155
just the way it's going to be?

00:07:36.155 --> 00:07:38.458
Every single day for the next two years?

00:07:38.791 --> 00:07:41.160
Or is this a moment where

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:42.361
there's not going to be a Kumbaya

00:07:42.361 --> 00:07:43.362
unity type thing,

00:07:43.362 --> 00:07:44.730
but people start to sit down

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:46.332
and realize we're going to have to start

00:07:46.332 --> 00:07:46.799
to govern?

00:07:46.799 --> 00:07:47.467
As Mel was saying,

00:07:47.467 --> 00:07:48.201
and we're going to have to start

00:07:48.201 --> 00:07:51.304
to figure out a way to make this work.

00:07:52.171 --> 00:07:53.706
How you define making this work,

00:07:53.706 --> 00:07:54.273
I think, is

00:07:54.273 --> 00:07:55.308
a pretty open question right now,

00:07:55.308 --> 00:07:58.044
because I can just tell you that nobody

00:07:58.044 --> 00:07:58.344
I don't want

00:07:58.344 --> 00:07:59.645
speak to the people at this table,

00:07:59.645 --> 00:08:00.379
but literally

00:08:00.379 --> 00:08:02.515
nobody thinks this is going to go well.

00:08:03.216 --> 00:08:04.817
Everyone is not based

00:08:04.817 --> 00:08:06.085
based on what we've seen.

00:08:06.085 --> 00:08:07.119
And so I just

00:08:07.119 --> 00:08:08.020
because there's a lot of questions

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:08.888
that come out of it.

00:08:08.888 --> 00:08:10.623
And I think that's why we can break down,

00:08:10.623 --> 00:08:10.957
you know,

00:08:10.957 --> 00:08:12.225
all the intricacies

00:08:12.225 --> 00:08:14.560
of the procedural things that happen.

00:08:14.861 --> 00:08:16.262
But at the bottom line,

00:08:16.262 --> 00:08:18.498
people have been watching from home

00:08:18.664 --> 00:08:19.599
all week.

00:08:19.599 --> 00:08:21.601
And to them, it looks like chaos.

00:08:21.601 --> 00:08:24.670
To them, it looks like a complete mess.

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:25.304
And to them,

00:08:25.304 --> 00:08:26.072
it looks like,

00:08:26.072 --> 00:08:26.806
you know, another

00:08:26.806 --> 00:08:29.208
symbol of government dysfunction

00:08:29.342 --> 00:08:30.276
and it doesn't bode

00:08:30.276 --> 00:08:31.677
well for the next two years.

00:08:31.677 --> 00:08:34.113
Again, what Melanie said about

00:08:34.113 --> 00:08:35.114
Speaker McCarthy

00:08:35.114 --> 00:08:37.583
now giving away a lot of his power,

00:08:37.783 --> 00:08:40.219
further empowering those far

00:08:40.219 --> 00:08:41.220
right members

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:42.488
to really

00:08:42.488 --> 00:08:43.623
be obstructionists

00:08:43.623 --> 00:08:45.525
any time they want to be.

00:08:45.525 --> 00:08:47.193
How is he going to get anything done?

